---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import report from '../../../../docs/benchmarks/results.json';
const pct = (n: number) => (n * 100).toFixed(1) + '%';
---

<Layout
  title="A measured look at field matching"
  description="Reproducible FormPilot benchmark results with explicit denominators, held-out synthetic cases, abstentions, errors and runtime measurements."
>
  <div class="page-heading">
    <h1>Show the work. Keep the caveats.</h1>
    <p>
      A small, reproducible benchmark of the actual matching engine. These synthetic examples test
      specific behaviors; they do not represent every website.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="grid-3" style="margin-bottom:35px">
    <div class="benchmark-stat">
      <div class="benchmark-number">{pct(report.heldOut.precision)}</div>
      <p class="small muted">Precision among proposed matches</p>
    </div>
    <div class="benchmark-stat">
      <div class="benchmark-number">{pct(report.heldOut.coverage)}</div>
      <p class="small muted">Coverage across eligible fields</p>
    </div>
    <div class="benchmark-stat">
      <div class="benchmark-number">{report.heldOut.incorrectHigh}</div>
      <p class="small muted">Incorrect high-confidence matches</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Measured {report.generatedAt}. Evaluation set: {report.heldOut.cases} fields across five
      scenarios, including {report.heldOut.eligible} eligible fields and {report.heldOut.excluded}{' '}
      expected exclusions. A separate development set contains {report.development.cases} cases.
    </p>
    <h2>Results by scenario</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Scenario</th>
            <th>Precision</th>
            <th>Coverage</th>
            <th>Abstention</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {Object.entries(report.byScenario).map(([name, r]) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{name}</td>
              <td>{pct(r.precision)}</td>
              <td>{pct(r.coverage)}</td>
              <td>{pct(r.abstentionRate)}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <h2>What the numbers mean</h2>
    <p>
      Precision is correct property proposals divided by all proposals (
      {report.heldOut.correctProposals}/{report.heldOut.proposed}). Coverage is eligible fields with
      a proposal divided by all eligible fields. Abstention rate is eligible fields without a
      proposal divided by all eligible fields: {pct(report.heldOut.abstentionRate)}. An expected
      exclusion is outside the eligible denominator. A proposal on an expected exclusion would still
      count as an incorrect proposal.
    </p>
    <p>
      Intentional abstentions are successful outcomes, not missed positive matches. The matcher
      correctly abstained on {report.heldOut.correctExpectedAbstentions} of{' '}
      {report.heldOut.expectedAbstentions} deliberately ambiguous eligible cases. Exclusion
      classification errors: {report.heldOut.exclusionErrors}. These categories are not calibrated
      probabilities.
    </p>
    <h2>Failures remain visible</h2>
    <p>
      The JSON report retains every mismatched expected outcome, including missing profile values. A
      conflicting autocomplete token can win over the visible label and still be wrong; the conflict
      is marked for review. This evaluation reports the proposed key, so a review warning does not
      erase an error.
    </p>
    <h2>Runtime, with context</h2>
    <p>
      Median {report.runtimeMs.median.toFixed(4)} ms and p95 {report.runtimeMs.p95.toFixed(4)} ms
      per field. Measured over {report.environment.timingSamples.toLocaleString()} calls after{' '}
      {report.environment.warmupCalls.toLocaleString()} warm-up calls, on {report.environment.cpu},{' '}
      {report.environment.platform} {report.environment.arch}, Node {report.environment.node}. This
      excludes DOM inspection, browser messaging, storage and rendering. It is not an end-to-end
      browser latency claim.
    </p>
    <h2>Reproduce and challenge it</h2>
    <pre><code>npm ci{'\n'}npm run benchmark</code></pre>
    <p>
      Cases are hand-authored English metadata examples. The development set comes from the five
      controlled demos; the held-out file was authored separately and frozen before the first
      benchmark. They are not random samples, independent third-party validation or a guarantee of
      real-site performance. Source and expected labels live in <code>packages/form-fixtures</code>.
      The report is written to <code>docs/benchmarks/results.json</code> and this page is rebuilt
      from it.
    </p>
    <p>
      The matching benchmark measures metadata decisions. Separate browser tests exercise
      React-controlled inputs, dynamic country fields, fill behavior and undo. A good matcher result
      alone does not prove a successful fill.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
